# What the Docker build context excludes.
#
# Docker does not read .gitignore, so this is a separate list for the same
# idea: what is generated rather than authored never enters the image. The
# image generates its own, so the build depends only on what is committed.
#
# The test is "does a tool generate this?", not "is it large". Two people with
# the same commit and different local directories must build the same image.

# The `deps` stage installs this from the lockfile. Copying the developer's
# tree here would overwrite that install with whatever is on the machine --
# measured: a sentinel file placed in the context's node_modules reaches the
# image through `COPY . .`. 187 MB on a normal checkout.
node_modules

# SvelteKit's generated types and routes, written by `svelte-kit sync`. Vite
# regenerates it on start, so the container never needs the host's copy, and a
# stale one from an older SvelteKit would be read instead of being rebuilt.
.svelte-kit

# The adapter's output. The container runs `vite dev`, which does not read it.
# Keeping it out also means a future switch to `node build/index.js` cannot
# silently serve a build produced on someone's laptop.
build

# Vite's own cache, when it exists.
.vite

# Artifacts of a test run, including failure screenshots and traces.
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report

# Local tool state, not part of the project.
.atl
